• The phrase "tastier than expected" suggests a comparison to the subject's prior expectations about the medicine's taste.
• This comparison implies that the subject was pleasantly surprised by the medicine's taste, which is consistent with option c, but option c is not the best fit because it says "pleasantly" which is not in the quote.

